peaking at $311.30 and pulling back 28% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Feb 28, 2019 it closed at $312.49, its first close above the base high of $311.30. Volume that day was 756K shares, 1.09x the prior 10-day average of 696K. It didn't hold. By Mar 11, 2019 it had closed below the breakout level three days running, and the chart ends at $347.30.","lesson":"This is an example of a shakeout. The breakout failed by the rules, closing below the level three days running, and then the stock recovered and ran. Cutting it was still the right call when it happened. A failed breakout that fixes itself is worth watching for a re-entry, not a reason to ignore the exit."}}